    "faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Slotted vs non-slotted beads?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Slotted beads open to the side so they seat on jig hooks and straight shanks. Standard through-hole beads slide over the hook eye.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Tungsten vs brass or glass — sink rate?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Tungsten is denser, so it sinks faster at a smaller diameter. Brass is a moderate sink. Glass is light and translucent when you want a visible head without much weight.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I match bead size to hook?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Use the sizing list on this page (~1.5 mm midges through ~8–9 mm Fathom). Size the bead so it sits flush behind the eye without crowding the thorax.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
